  "term": "seasonal mood disorder",
  "definition": "Seasonal mood disorder is a recurring pattern in which depressive episodes come back at a similar time each year, most commonly in the winter. It can also involve anxiety, irritability, low energy, sleeping longer than usual, eating more with cravings for carbohydrates, and gaining weight.",
